17:["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.04] p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-300","children":"Why the tick is 2 seconds"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400","children":"An earlier draft of this document banned automation outright. Playtesting killed it: on a 6-inch screen, a thumb parked on an attack pad is a thumb that cannot also read the floor, and the player ends up watching their own hands instead of the telegraph."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400","children":["So baseline damage moved onto a metronome — and the metronome was made deliberately slow. Two seconds is roughly one wind-up window, which means there is always room to act ",["$","em",null,{"children":"between"}]," ticks. The skill ceiling is preserved because any manual ability resets the tick: pressing buttons is always strictly faster than not pressing them. Automation sets the floor. It never touches the ceiling."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.04] p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-300","children":"The death contract"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-400","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-rose-300","children":"−10% experience."}]," Enough to erase an evening. Never enough to erase a character."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-amber-300","children":"−50% carried gold."}]," Banked gold at the Sanctuary is safe. Deciding when to walk home ",["$","em",null,{"children":"is"}]," the risk system."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-sky-300","children":"A Remnant spawns."}]," Your dropped gold lands on the floor, locked to you for 60 seconds. Get back inside that window and it is yours. Miss it and it belongs to whoever is standing there."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-emerald-300","children":"Equipped gear is safe"}]," outside Emberfield and the Grey Barrow, which are labelled at the border."]}]]}]]}]]}]
18:["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400","children":"Shove is the answer to the 'nowhere to run' problem in a grid game. Instead of only moving yourself, you can move the board. Crucially it interrupts a telegraph in progress, which makes it a defensive cooldown with a positional payoff: shove a Grave Wraith out of its own 3×3 bloom and you have both dodged and repositioned it for a Cleave."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-1.5","children":[["$","li","Same gesture on both platforms: touch drag, or mouse hold-left-click and release.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"Same gesture on both platforms: touch drag, or mouse hold-left-click and release."]}],["$","li","Exactly 1 tile. Destination must be walkable, unoccupied and not inside the Sanctuary.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"Exactly 1 tile. Destination must be walkable, unoccupied and not inside the Sanctuary."]}],["$","li","You must be adjacent to the creature. 2.5s cooldown; creature is braced for 1.2s after.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"You must be adjacent to the creature. 2.5s cooldown; creature is braced for 1.2s after."]}],["$","li","Cancels an in-progress wind-up and deletes the telegraph — the whole reason it exists.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"Cancels an in-progress wind-up and deletes the telegraph — the whole reason it exists."]}],["$","li","A live arrow preview paints the destination cyan (valid) or red (invalid) before you release.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"A live arrow preview paints the destination cyan (valid) or red (invalid) before you release."]}]]}]]}]
19:["$","article","armor",{"className":"rounded-3xl border border-sky-500/40 bg-white/[0.04] p-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-3xl","children":"🛡️"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"min-w-[200px] flex-1","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-black text-slate-50","children":"Gear slots & flat armour"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm font-medium text-amber-300/90","children":"Eight slots. Armour rating is the sum of equipped pieces and reduces physical damage by a flat value."}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400","children":"Percentage mitigation is unreadable on a phone — nobody computes 23% of 17 mid-telegraph. Flat mitigation is arithmetic a player does automatically: 17 damage against 6 armour is 11, every single time. That predictability is what lets a player decide to eat a hit rather than dodge it, which is the decision that makes armour interesting."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-1.5","children":[["$","li","Slots: head, neck, chest, weapon, off-hand, legs, feet, ring.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"Slots: head, neck, chest, weapon, off-hand, legs, feet, ring."]}],["$","li","damage = max(1, raw − armour). Armour can never fully negate a hit.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"damage = max(1, raw − armour). Armour can never fully negate a hit."]}],["$","li","Damage numbers show the reduction inline: '11 (-6)'.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"Damage numbers show the reduction inline: '11 (-6)'."]}],["$","li","Heavy armour adds encumbrance: +5ms per point to the grid step, capped at +90ms.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"Heavy armour adds encumbrance: +5ms per point to the grid step, capped at +90ms."]}],["$","li","Ember Plate is 12 armour and 8 encumbrance — best mitigation, worst footwork.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"Ember Plate is 12 armour and 8 encumbrance — best mitigation, worst footwork."]}]]}]]}]]}]
1a:["$","article","loot",{"className":"rounded-3xl border border-amber-500/40 bg-white/[0.04] p-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-3xl","children":"✦"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"min-w-[200px] flex-1","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-black text-slate-50","children":"Loot: spread, claim, filter"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm font-medium text-amber-300/90","children":"Drops scatter over 1 sqm, lock to the top damage dealer for 60 seconds, and are hidden entirely if your filter excludes them."}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400","children":"Three separate problems solved by three separate rules. Spread stops a nine-item drop becoming an unreadable pile on one 44px tile. The 60-second claim stops the highest-level player in the zone from stealing every kill they did not earn. The filter is the mobile clarity valve: if you are farming Grave Silk, sewer pelts should not be drawn on your screen at all."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-1.5","children":[["$","li","Drops distribute across the walkable 3×3 around the corpse, corpse tile first.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"Drops distribute across the walkable 3×3 around the corpse, corpse tile first."]}],["$","li","Top damage dealer holds an exclusive 60s claim; a lock icon and countdown arc render on the stack.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"Top damage dealer holds an exclusive 60s claim; a lock icon and countdown arc render on the stack."]}],["$","li","After 60s the stack is free for anyone. Ground items decay after 3 minutes.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"After 60s the stack is free for anyone. Ground items decay after 3 minutes."]}],["$","li","Filtered-out items are not drawn, not tappable, and skipped by auto pick-up.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"Filtered-out items are not drawn, not tappable, and skipped by auto pick-up."]}],["$","li","Auto pick-up takes claimable, filtered loot the moment you step onto its tile.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"Auto pick-up takes claimable, filtered loot the moment you step onto its tile."]}]]}]]}]]}]
1b:["$","article","pz",{"className":"rounded-3xl border border-emerald-500/40 bg-white/[0.04] p-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-3xl","children":"🕊️"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"min-w-[200px] flex-1","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-black text-slate-50","children":"Protected zones"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm font-medium text-amber-300/90","children":"Inside a Protected Zone creatures cannot land damage and PvP is hard-blocked. You may still attack out."}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400","children":"The Sanctuary is the only place in the world where the risk system switches off, and it has to be absolute: any ambiguity about whether you are safe makes banking loot feel like a gamble rather than a reward. Note the deliberate asymmetry requested for the slice — you can attack out of a PZ but nothing can attack in."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-1.5","children":[["$","li","Creatures may not path into a PZ and may not resolve damage against a player inside one.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"Creatures may not path into a PZ and may not resolve damage against a player inside one."]}],["$","li","PvP attacks are rejected outright inside a PZ. No exceptions, no flagging.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"PvP attacks are rejected outright inside a PZ. No exceptions, no flagging."]}],["$","li","You may attack creatures standing outside the PZ from within it.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"You may attack creatures standing outside the PZ from within it."]}],["$","li","Shoving a creature into a PZ is blocked — otherwise it becomes an untouchable-mob exploit.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"Shoving a creature into a PZ is blocked — otherwise it becomes an untouchable-mob exploit."]}],["$","li","The zone border is drawn as a dashed gold ring, labelled, and shown on the HUD.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-xs text-slate-300","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-amber-400","children":"▸"}],"The zone border is drawn as a dashed gold ring, labelled, and shown on the HUD."]}]]}]]}]]}]
1c:["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-3xl border border-rose-500/30 bg-rose-500/5 p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-rose-300","children":"Known open issues these rules create"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500","children":"A design bible that only lists wins is a sales deck. These are live and unresolved."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","div","PZ safe-spotting is currently exploitable",{"className":"rounded-2xl bg-black/40 p-4","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-xs font-black text-slate-100","children":"PZ safe-spotting is currently exploitable"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-[11px] leading-relaxed text-slate-400","children":"Attack-out / no-attack-in means a player can stand on the Sanctuary border and freely kill anything that wanders adjacent. Shipping mitigation: creatures leash and disengage after 4 seconds of being unable to reach their attacker, and regenerate to full. Implemented in the slice: creatures will not path adjacent to the PZ, and cannot be shoved into it."}]]}],["$","div","Auto-attack weakens the anti-bot argument",{"className":"rounded-2xl bg-black/40 p-4","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-xs font-black text-slate-100","children":"Auto-attack weakens the anti-bot argument"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-[11px] leading-relaxed text-slate-400","children":"A 2s tick is trivially automatable, so combat is no longer inherently bot-hostile. The load moves to telegraph dodging and shove usage — telemetry now flags accounts with abnormally low damage-taken-per-hour alongside high tick counts."}]]}],["$","div","Loot filters hide items from the economy",{"className":"rounded-2xl bg-black/40 p-4","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-xs font-black text-slate-100","children":"Loot filters hide items from the economy"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-[11px] leading-relaxed text-slate-400","children":"If most players filter out common materials, those materials stop entering the market and low-level crafting stalls. We watch the ratio of dropped-to-collected per item and adjust drop rates, not filters — the filter must stay a pure player-clarity tool."}]]}]]}]]}]
